<title>USA: NEBRASKA FED CATTLE $105-$106/DRESSED - PRIVATE.</title>
<headline>NEBRASKA FED CATTLE $105-$106/DRESSED - PRIVATE.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nebraska feedlot cattle trade near midday Wednesday was light to moderate at $105.00 to $106.00 per cwt on a dressed basis, steady to up $1.00 from sales so far this week, market sources said.</p>
<p>About 10,000 to 15,000 head traded, which brought the week to date figure near 82,000, the sources said.</p>
<p>Sales on a live basis were at $65.00 to $66.00, also steady to up $1.00 from earlier in the week, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;I think today's trade will clean up the week's showlist,&quot; one market source said.</p>
<p>This week's showlist had been estimated near 93,000 head.</p>
<p>((Bob Janis 312-983-7347))</p>
